        "id": 1229339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-14T00:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think this should be: 0x8c0 bytes (0xe3000 - 0xe2740). The 0xe2740 comes from the Offset field of the .data.rel.ro section from the section table.\n\n0x41b40 + 0xa0bf0 sums to 0xe2730, which is the end of the .plt section, but there\u0027s a 16-byte gap between the end of .plt and the start of .data.rel.ro. It\u0027s needed to accommodate .data.rel.ro\u0027s 32-byte alignment.",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 79,
        "startChar": 11,
        "endLine": 79,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "89dcdb7652db98f0e6c7925f5e48f7a7f17f4bbd",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889",
      "unresolved": true
    },
    {
      "key": {
        "uuid": "7209e7c7_0215fd85",
        "filename": "/COMMIT_MSG",
        "patchSetId": 4
      },
      "lineNbr": 84,
      "author": {
        "id": 1229339
      },
      "writtenOn": "2019-12-14T00:29:14Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think these terms need to be flipped around. The (0x41b40 + 0xa0bf0) is the offset+size of the third segment, but maybe it\u0027d be clearer to use the offset+size of the .plt section? That would look like:\n\n    0x0e0800 + 0x001f30\n\nBoth expressions evaluate to 0xe2730, the end of .plt.\n\ne.g. I\u0027d suggest:\n\n((0x0e0800 + 0x001f30) - 0xe2000)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 84,
        "startChar": 23,
        "endLine": 84,
        "endChar": 54
      },
      "revId": "89dcdb7652db98f0e6c7925f5e48f7a7f17f4bbd",
